{"kind":"request","text":"Archive: defer for capacity instead of stopping.\nToday a pass with no affordable candidate returns limit (archive-adaptive.ts:207), and the driver then stores the row as stopped with reason limit. Nothing restarts a stopped row. This is the likely cause of the stopped row on object c7a17b72 on dap-grow.\nWork, as proposed in 6ffc771a: add an internal deferred-for-capacity result. Return it only for a limited lookahead, or for a non-null finish quote with canSpend false, before a prefix is selected. The driver then retries on its existing wake. It does not refund cost and does not create a Mark. A null cost, invalid data and a failed exact rebuild of a pending Mark stay stopped.","body":{"conditions":"(1) A witness shows that a capacity shortage defers and retries, and does not store a stop. (2) A witness shows that each hard refusal still stops. (3) The retry uses the existing backoff and wake arbitration; no new alarm. (4) Gate once before review. (5) Exact-head checker review before the planner deploys.","priority":"high","target":"inherit","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}